# Packages
> `upkg` installs add-ons from the UP-Term feed on GitHub. It needs a network and
> the base UP-Term installed. This lesson only types the lines; nothing is installed.
>   upkg update              fetch the feed's package list
>   upkg list                the packages the feed offers
>   upkg install NAME        install an add-on
>   upkg upgrade             bring the installed add-ons up to the feed
>   upkg remove NAME         remove an add-on
? Fetch the package list with upkg update.
= case "$LEARN_LINE" in "upkg update") true ;; *) false ;; esac
~ Type upkg update.
! upkg update
? List the packages the feed offers.
= case "$LEARN_LINE" in "upkg list") true ;; *) false ;; esac
~ Type upkg list.
! upkg list
